    keyword520: "Abnormal water supply of clean water tank ",
    keyword521: "Solutions:\r\n1. Ensure the main water valve is open, the three-way valve is open, and the household water supply is not cut off.\r\n2. Ensure the three-way valve connection point is not loose; if loose, tighten the connection point.\r\n3. Ensure the pressure reducing valve connection point is not installed backward; if backward, reinstall it correctly.",
    keyword522: "Abnormal water releasing of clean water tank",
    keyword523: "Solutions:\r\n1. Ensure the auto water refill and drain kit is properly installed, with the top of the module level with the top of the base station.\r\n2. If the installation is correct but the “Abnormal water reflling of clean water tank” message still appears, please contact customer service.",
    keyword524: "Abnormal pumping of the used water tank",
    keyword525: "Solutions:\r\n1. Ensure the suction pipe in the mop cleaning slot is in contact with the water surface; if bent, adjust it to normal.\r\n2. Ensure the used water tank lid is completely closed and the tank can maintain a sealed state.\r\n3. Ensure the check valve assembly is not missing; if missing, install it in the direction of the arrow.",
    keyword526: "Abnormal drainage of the used water tank",
    keyword527: "Solutions:\r\n1. Ensure the drainage tube of auto water refill and drain kit is inserted into the floor drain or wall drain.\r\n2. Ensure the drain or wall drain is not clogged; if clogged, clean and unclog it.\r\n3. Ensure the check valve assembly is not installed backward; if backward, reinstall it in the direction of the arrow.",
